[issue.1743]
number = 1743
title = "[Coherence] The production daemon's native-read 503 body now includes a Debug dump of the internal error, which contradicts the serve-errors contract and the module's own no-behaviour-change claim"
revision = "a910fdedd579e63379ae6c2e4d4971990d28f8ad"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "Commit 76589ba8624594fd1047bbe77ec4a4ee027082fc introduced the still-present Debug detail at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/proof_native_reads.rs:235, compiled into the executable by services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/main.rs:197 and services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/proof_serve_errors.rs:14, exposing the nested Connection error at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/read/native.rs:19 and RPC message/data at services/agent/crates/layerx-client/src/sequencer.rs:66 despite the code-only body in contracts/agent-api.md:159 and spec/layerx-merge/contracts/agent-api.md:1021, while services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/proof_serve_errors.rs:11 claims unchanged semantics and its decoder at :126 requires the diagnostic field."
close_comment = "Native-read failures currently expose internal diagnostics and upstream RPC error text in the listener response. Restore the fixed 503 body {\"error\":\"verified_read_unavailable\"} and add regression coverage that rejects diagnostic fields while preserving the existing error codes and status mappings."

